Z||000000||ezsurf||08-09-2001||06:37 PM||||I have a question for any exhaust experts out there. I have an 86SE with a V6 engine.  The exhaust pipe that leads from the Y pipe to the catalytic converter does not have any support tabs on it.  There are support tabs with support springs on the passenger side of the car, but not on the drivers side.  There are support tabs on the cradle on the drivers side, but not on the pipe.  Additionally, I have the Pontiac shop manual, and it does not show any support tabs on the pipe either.  It would seem this is an aftermarket pipe, however, I am 90% sure that this is the original exhaust.  If you have an 86 model with a V6, tell me what your car has on it.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||08-09-2001||07:20 PM||||My car had the original exhaust on it last month. (recently went to an Ocelot system) I had 3 support springs at the output of the Y pipe where it curves to the Cat, I had 3 of them at the bend after the Cat, and 6 of them holding the muffler. My car is an 86 SE V-6 <P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">     <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 08-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||ezsurf||08-09-2001||08:44 PM||||Thanks Oreif.  I now know what has been done to the car.  The pipe immediately after the Y pipe and the catalytic converter have been replaced.  The rest of the exhaust system is stock.||||reg||1
